WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.290
- [Robin] From the belly of
production, there's a hallway

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:04.630
that leads into the studio.

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:07.950
I liken it to the pathway
that players walk through

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:09.523
to get out on to the field.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:13.300
That live element is never lost on us.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.920
You're hosting a show while working out,

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.350
while engaging with thousands of people.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.240
When that producer counts me down,
there's nothing but go.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.490
(intense action music)

00:00:38.127 --> 00:00:40.090
I grew up in an immigrant family.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.600
My mother was a refugee from Cuba,

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.880
my father from Puerto Rico,

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.010
and they really created themselves.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:47.360
My mother was an example
of a superhero for me.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.330
She paved the way for me to say, “yeah,

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:50.960
“you can write your own story.”

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.390
I really am a walking
example of how you can

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:56.320
reframe the direction of your life.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:57.720
I did not grow up an athlete.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:58.950
I was the arts-and-craft kid.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:00.250
I was the kid who was good at school,

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.030
and I didn't know why I felt so compelled

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:03.940
to physically just put one
foot in front of the other;

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:06.310
but I was in law school,
and one day I was like,

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:08.663
maybe I'll run home
instead of driving home.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.453
For me, that unlocked powers
that I never knew I had.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:18.140
I realized that when you
step into your power,

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.380
it gives people permission
to do the same thing.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.940
So if I can be a small catalyst in that,

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:25.777
I damn near try every
single day on the bike.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.090
Peloton instructors are required

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:34.090
to put so much energy into
every ride, into every workout.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.310
We actually have to train
like professional athletes

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:37.930
to teach.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.310
The instructor is not
just a body on a bike.

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:42.530
They are the conductor of an orchestra.

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:44.660
A lot of people don't know
that instructors spend

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:46.810
hours for every single playlist.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.610
For every 30 or 45 minutes of music,

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:51.570
an instructor has spent hours
curating that journey.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.080
There is an element to what we produce

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.090
that is truly a show.

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:58.270
There's lighting, there's
music, there's levels.

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:01.190
Our production department
rivals any network.

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:03.270
We produce 14 hours of live programming

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:04.580
from our studio in New York City,

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:08.690
and we broadcast to thousands
of bikes across the country.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.910
Other members can see
and high-five each other

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:12.370
and see themselves on the leaderboard

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:14.340
and keeps them coming back.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.120
We're doing something that's
never been done before,

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:17.720
and people are responding to it.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.690
I received a message
from a mother who said

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:22.950
thank you so much for your 20-minute ride

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.310
'cause I can feel like
a badass during nap-time.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:26.940
Like, I really am stronger
than I thought I was.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.880
I was like that mic-drop, bye queen.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.490
Do you know how amazing
it is what you just did?

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:35.990
I really truly approach
every ride hoping that

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:39.080
it plants a seed of
strength in someone's life.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.110
I want people to leave my class

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:43.393
feeling like they
stepped into their power.

